pal sources of income (+) or loss (-) for the fund are profits (+) or\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 266, 1486, 332], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"losses (-) on SDRs and for eign ex change, as well as in ter est earned on as sets.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 342, 1495, 618], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-1 presentsthe assets, liabilities and capital of the fund. The fig ures are in U.S. dol lars or their equiv alents based on current exchange rates computed ac cord ing to the ac- crual method of ac count ing. The capi tal ac count represents the original capital appr opri ated to the fund by Congress of $2 bil- lion, mi nus a sub se quent trans fer of $1.8 bil lion to pay for the ini tial U.S. quota sub scription to the In ter na tional Mon e tary Fund. Gains and losses are re flected in the cu mu la tive net in- come (+) or loss (-) ac count.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 625, 1484, 747], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-2 shows the results of operations by quarter. Figures are in U.S. dollars or their equivalent computed according to the accrual method. \\\"Profit (+) or loss (-) on foreign exchange\\\" includes realized profits or losses. \\\"Adjusted\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [379, 844, 1251, 882], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"TABLE ESF-1.\\u2014Bal ances as of July 1, 2000, and Sept. 30, 2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [461, 898, 1171, 924], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"[In thou sands of dol lars. Source: Of fice of the As sis tant Sec re tary of the Trea sury for Man agement]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 966, 1479, 1876], \"page_id\": 112}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>As set