"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [709, 87, 907, 132], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1443, 90, 1488, 127], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"127\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [474, 186, 1155, 236], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Nuclear Waste Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 240, 805, 474], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"The Nu clear Waste Fund was es tab lished on the books of the Trea sury in fis cal 1983, ac cord ing to sec tion 302 of the Nu- clear Waste Pol icy Act of 1982 [Pub lic Law 97-425, cod ified at 42 United States Code 10222(c)]. Receipts repre sent fees col lected from public util i ties based on elec tric ity gen erated by nu clear power re ac tors and spent nu clear fuel. Ex pen di- tures from the fund are for pur poses of ra dio ac tive waste dis- posal activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 471, 801, 596], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"Amounts avail able in the fund ex ceed ing cur rent needs may be in vested by the Sec retary of the Treasury in ob liga tions of the United States (1) hav ing ma tu ri ties in tan dem with the needs of the waste fund and (2) bear ing in ter est at rates de ter-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 245, 1503, 410], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"mined appropriate, taking into consideration the current average market yield on outstanding marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to the maturities of such in vestments, except that the interest rate on such in vestments shall not exceed the average interest rate applicable to existing borrowings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 410, 1506, 585], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of the Department of Energy (DOE), is required by 42 United States Code 10222(e)(1). This report must present the financial condition and the results of operations of the waste fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [546, 632, 1091, 712], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"TA BLE TF-18.\\u2014Nu clear Waste Fund Results of Oper a tions, Fiscal 2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [761, 728, 876, 761], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOE]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [126, 759, 1497, 1876], \"page_id\": 124}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1999</td><td>$1,145,354</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>701,645,045</td></tr><tr><td>Penalties and interest on fee payments</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>883,215,008</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>1,584,860,053</td></tr><tr><td>Nonexpenditure transfers:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>SF-1151 transfers in (+)</td><td>227,423,413</td></tr><tr><td>SF-1151 transfers out (-)</td><td>245,173,413</td></tr><tr><td>Net nonexpenditure transfers</td><td>-17,750,000</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DOE radio active waste disposal activities</td><td>268,037,685</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of investments</td><td>1,294,855,212</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>1,562,892,897</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2000</td><td>$5,362,510</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 85, 199, 127], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"128\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [705, 78, 922, 127], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [413, 191, 1206, 236], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Reforestation Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 245, 798, 417], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"The Reforestation Trust Fund was established on the books of the Trea sury in fis cal 1981 to con tinue through Sep-tem ber 30, 1985, ac cord ing to pro vi sions of Title III\\u2014Re for-estation, of the Recreational Boating Safety and Facilities Improve ment Act of 1980 [Pub lic Law 96-451, cod i fied at 16 United States Code 1606a(a)].\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 420, 803, 691], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"The act pro vides that the Sec re tary of the Trea sury shall trans fer to the trust fund tariffs, lim ited to not more than $30 million for any fiscal year, rece ived in the Trea sury from Oc to- ber 1, 1979, through Sep tem ber 30, 1985, on (1) rough and pri- mary wood products and wood waste; (2) lumber, floor ing and moldings; and (3) wood veneers, plywood, other wood-veneer assem blies and building boards. Public Law 99-190, ti tle II, 99 Stat utes at Large 1245, ex tended the re- ceipts for the trust fund. Amounts avail able in the re fores tation\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [827, 238, 1495, 387], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"trust fund exceeding current withdrawals are invested in interest-bearing obligations of the United States or in obligations guaranteed as to both principal and interest by the United States. The interest on, and the proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligations are credited to the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 391, 1508, 523], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Department of Agriculture is authorized to obligate available sums in the trust fund (including any amounts not obligated in previous years) for (1) reforestation and timber stand improvement and (2) administrative costs of the Government for these activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [816, 521, 1499, 698], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"An nual re ports are re quired by 16 United States Code 1606a(c)(1) to be sub mitted by the Sec re tary of the Trea sury, after con sul ta tion with the Sec re tary of Ag ri cul ture, on the fi- nancial con di tion and the re sults of the op er a tions of the trust fund dur ing the past fis cal year and on its ex pected con di tion and oper a tions dur ing the next fis cal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [510, 754, 1126, 846], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-19.\\u2014Reforestation Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [685, 865, 949, 889], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"[Source:Department of Agriculture]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 903, 1503, 1329], \"page_id\": 125}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1999</td><td>$8,265,582</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excisetaxes(tariffs)</td><td>30,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Redemptionofinvestment</td><td>245,212</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>30,245,212</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>13,200,284</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>13,200,284</td></tr><tr><td>Adjustment</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2000</td><td>$25,310,510</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [397, 