, \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturity ties for bills, notes and bonds. The Treasury yield curve in the accompanying chart is based on current market bid quotations on the most actively traded Treasury securities as of 3:30 p.m. on the last business day of the calendar quarter.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [129, 568, 794, 759], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"The Treasury uses quotations obtained by the FRB of New York to de rive the yield curve, based on semi an nual in-terest pay ments and read at con stant ma tu rity points to de-volve a consistent data series. Yields on Treasury bills are coupon equivalent yields of bank discount rates at which Trea sury bills trade in the mar ket. The Board of Gov er nors of\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 288, 1492, 342], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"the Federal Reserve System publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly H.15 press release.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 351, 1492, 721], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"Table MY-2 shows average yields of long-term Treasury, corporate and municipal bonds. The long-term Treasury average yield is the 30-year constant maturity yield. The corporate bond average yield is developed by Treasury by calculating reoffering yields on new long-term securities maturing in at least 20 years and rated Aa by Moody\\u2019s Investors Service. The municipal bond average yield prior to 1991 was compiled by Treasury. Beginning with January 1991, the average yield is the \\u201cMunicipal Bond Yield Average,\\u201d published by Moody\\u2019s Investors Service for 20-year reoffering yields on selected Aa-rated general obligations. See the foot notes for further explanation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"co