n\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [437, 365, 1175, 398], \"page_id\": 114}], \"content\": \"*Note.\\u2014Data was not avail able at the time of pub li ca tion.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 87, 193, 120], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"118\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [716, 92, 905, 118], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [410, 177, 1226, 271], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 278, 811, 533], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"The Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund was es tab lished on the books of Trea sury in fis cal 1993, ac cord ing to pro vi sions of the Eneryg Policy Act of 1992 (42 United States Code 2297g). Re ceipts rep re sent (1) fees col lected from do mes tic pub lic util i ties based on their pro rata share of pur chases of sep a ra tive work units from the De - part ment of Eneryg (DOE) and (2) ap pro pri a tions to ward the Government contribu tion based on the balance of sepa rate work unit pur chases.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 533, 805, 849], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"Ex pen di tures from the fund are for the pur pose of (1) de-contaminationand de com mis sion ing of the three gas eous dif-fu sion plants, (2) re me dial ac tions and re lat ed en vi ron men tal restoration costs at the gas eous dif fu sion plants and (3) re im - bursement to ura nium/tho rium pro duc ers for the costs of de - contamination, de commissioning, reclama tion and remedial ac tion of ura nium/tho rium sites that are in ci dent to sales to the U.S. Government. Amounts available in the fund exceeding cur rent needs may be in vested by the Sec re tary of the Tre a sury in ob li ga tions of the United States (1) hav ing ma tu ri ties con- gru ent with the needs of the fund and (2) bear ing in ter est at\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 278, 1495, 391], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"rates determined appropriate, taking into consideration the current average market yield on outstanding marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to these investments.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 394, 1495, 535], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Treasury is required by 42 United States Code 2297g(b)(1) to provide an annual report to Congress, after consultation with the Secretary of Energy. This report must present the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 533, 1490, 867], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"The Energy Policy Act of 1992 (42 United States Code 2297g-1, as amended) authorizes funding to ensure an equal deposit to the fund of $488.3 million before adjustments for inflation. The Act stipulates that the Government deposit $338.3 million, adjusted for inflation, annually. The Act also calls for deposits of $150 million from domestic public utility assessments. Between the fiscal years of 1993 and 2000, the total Government contribution amount authorized by the Act was $2,844.0 million. During that time span, the Government contributed only $2,283.6 million to the fund. The resulting shortfall in authorized Government contributions is, therefore, $560.4 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [224, 882, 1401, 955], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-11.\\u2014Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [752, 966, 871, 992], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOE]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 995, 1495, 1414], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1999</td><td>$298</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>594,760,328</td></tr><tr><td>Penalties collected</td><td>8,899</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>124,080,159</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>718,849,386</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DOE, decontamination and decommissioning activities</td><td>243,083,215</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of investments</td><td>475,766,391</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>718,849,606</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2000</td><td>$78</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [224, 1447, 1404, 1518], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-11.\\u2014Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal 2001-2005\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [670, 1527, 958, 1558], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"[In thou sands of dol lars. Source: DOE]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 1560, 1488, 1975], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2001</th><th>2002</th><th>2003</th><th>2004</th><th>2005</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"6\\\">Receipts:</td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>600,720</td><td>605,509</td><td>610,425</td><td>615,472</td><td>620,652</td></tr><tr><td>Interest collected</td><td>154,406</td><td>180,949</td><td>202,037</td><td>224,474</td><td>234,729</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>755,126</td><td>786,458</td><td>812,462</td><td>839,946</td><td>855,381</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"6\\\">Outlays:</td></tr><tr><td>DOE, decontamination and decommissioning fund.</td><td>274,000</td><td>277,300</td><td>407,967</td><td>409,567</td><td>658,667</td></tr><tr><td>Costs of investments</td><td>481,126</td><td>509,158</td><td>404,495</td><td>430,379</td><td>196,714</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>755,126</td><td>786,458</td><td>812,462</td><td>839,946</td><td>855,381</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [718, 92, 909, 123], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1443, 92, 1490, 123], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"119\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [366, 193, 1260, 238], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Black Lung Disability Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 245, 798, 412], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"The Black Lung Disability Trust Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1978 according to the Black Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1977 (Public Law 95-227). The Black Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1981 (Public Law 97-119) reestablished the fund in the Internal Revenue Code (IRC), 26 United States Code 9501.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 415, 798, 698], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"The Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985 (Public Law 99-272), enacted April 7, 1986, provided for an increase in the coal tax effective April 1, 1986, through December 31, 1995, and a 5-year for give ness of interest retroactive to October 1, 1985. The 5-year moratorium on interest payments ended on September 30, 1990. Payment of interest on advances resumed in fiscal 1991. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100-203, title X, section 10503), signed December 22, 1987, extends the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 695, 798, 877], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"The Code des ignates the fol low ing re ceipts to be ap pro-pri ated and trans ferred from the gen eral fund of the Trea sury to the trust fund: ex cise taxes on mined coal; tax able ex pen di-tures of self-dealing by, and ex cess con tri bu tions to, pri vate blacklung bene fit trusts; re imburse ments by re spon si ble mine oper a tors; and re lated fines, pen al ties and in terest charges.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 245, 1495, 358], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Es ti mates made by the Sec re tary of the Trea sury de ter mine monthly trans fers of amounts for ex cise taxes to the trust fund sub ject to ad just ments in later trans fers to ac tual tax re ceipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 356, 1495, 554], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"After retirement of the current indebtedness, amounts avail able in the fund ex ceed ing current ex pen di ture re quire ments will be in vested by the Sec re tary of the Trea sury in in terest-bearing pub lic debt se curi ties. Any in terest earned will be cred ited to the fund. Also cred ited, if nec es sary, will be re payable ad vances from the gen eral fund to meet out lay re quirements ex ceeding avail able re venues.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 549, 1495, 698], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"To carry out the program, amounts are made available to the Department of Labor (DOL). Also charged to the fund are administrative expenses incurred by the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) and the Treasury, repayments of advances from the general fund and interest on advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 695, 1494, 893], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"The Code requires the Secretary of the Treasury to submit an annual report to Congress after consultation with the Secretary of Labor and the Secretary of HHS [26 United States Code 9602(a)]. The report must present the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and the expected condition and operations of the fund during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [461, 959, 1169, 1030], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-12.\\u2014Black Lung Disability Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1051, 1492, 1930], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">[Source: DOL]</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1999</td><td>$20,083,189</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excisetaxes ( transferred from general fund):</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>$1.10 tax on un der ground coal</td><td>114,361,000</td></tr><tr><td>$0.55 tax on sur face coal</td><td>129,570,000</td></tr><tr><td>4.4 per cent tax on un der ground coal</td><td>194,084,000</td></tr><tr><td>4.4 per cent tax on sur face coal</td><td>80,452,000</td></tr><tr><td>Fines,penalties and interest</td><td>1,772,769</td></tr><tr><td>Collection\\u2014responsiblenameoperators</td><td>5,546,024</td></tr><tr><td>Re cov ery of prior year funds</td><td>131,000</td></tr><tr><td>Re payable advances from the gen eral fund</td><td>490,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>1,