l, \"id\": 56, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1455, 106, 1492, 141], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"33\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 203, 1177, 243], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Public Debt Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 288, 800, 592], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Chapter 31 of Title 31 of the United States Code allows the Secretary of Treasury to borrow money by issuing Treasury securities. The Secretary determines the terms and conditions of issue, conversion, maturity, payment and interest rate. New issues of Treasury notes mature in 2 to 10 years. Bonds mature in more than 10 years from the issue date. Each outstanding marketable security is listed in the \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\\\" The information in this section of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" pertains only to marketable Treasury securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 592, 801, 806], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-1 provides a maturity schedule of interest-bearing marketable Treasury notes and bonds. All unmatured Treasury notes and bonds are listed in maturity order, from earliest to latest. A separate breakout is provided for the combined holdings of the Government accounts and Federal Reserve Banks (FRBs), so that the \\\"all other investors\\\" category includes all private holdings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 808, 800, 870], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-2 presents the results of weekly auctions of 4-, 13- and 26-week bills. Treasury bills mature each Thurs-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 285, 1492, 441], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"day. Issues of 4- and 13-week bills are reopenings of 26-week bills. Issues of cash management bills also are presented. High yields on accepted tenders and the dollar value of total bids are presented, with the dollar value of awards made on both competitive and noncompetitive bases.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 443, 1494, 556], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"To encourage the participation of individuals and smaller institutions, Treasury accepts noncompetitive tenders of up to $1 million for bills and $5 million for notes and bonds in each auction of securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 563, 1492, 658], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-3 lists the results of auctions of marketable securities, other than weekly bills, in chronological order over the past 2 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 658, 1494, 806], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-4 indicates the total amount of marketable securities allotted to each class of investor. The FRBs tally into investor classes the tenders in each auction of marketable securities other than weekly auctions of 4-, 13- and 26-week bills.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [372, 889, 1246, 931], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [508, 952, 1126, 985], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"[Source: Bureau of the Public Debt, Office of Financing]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1009, 800, 1134], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On July 23, 2001, Treasury announced plans to begin regular weekly offerings of 4-week bills. The first 4-week bill was announced July 30, auctioned July 31 and issued August 2.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1193, 308, 1226], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"OCTOBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1245, 688, 1275], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 30-1/2-Year Inflation-Indexed Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1285, 801, 1457], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On October 3, 2001, Treasury announced it would auction $5,000 million of 30-1/2-year inflation-indexed bonds to raise cash. The 30-1/2-year inflation-indexed bonds of April 2032 were dated and issued October 15, 2001. They are due April 15, 2032, with interest payable on April 15 and October 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1457, 798, 1740], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 11 a.m. eastern daylight time (e.d.t) for noncompetitive tenders and before 11:30 a.m. e.d.t. for competitive tenders on October 10. Tenders totaled $11,156 million; Treasury accepted $5,000 million at the high yield of 3.465 percent with an equivalent price of 98.314. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 79.48 percent. The median yield was 3.420 percent, and the low yield was 3.300 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $88 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $4,912 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1744, 794, 1798], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of inflation-indexed bonds is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1817, 537, 1848], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 9-year 10-Month Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1855, 800, 1916], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On October 4, Treasury announced it would auction $6,000 million of 9-year 10-month notes to raise cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 1009, 1494, 1183], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"The 9-year 10-month 5 percent notes of Series C-2011 were dated August 15, 2001 and issued October 5, 2001. They are due August 15, 2011, with interest payable on February 15 and August 15 until maturity. Accrued interest of $6.92935 per $1,000, covering the period from August 15 to October 5, 2001, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 1183, 1497, 1582], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.d.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.t. for competitive tenders on October 5. Tenders totaled $14,175 million; Treasury accepted $6,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.519 percent with an equivalent price of 103.783. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 53.57 percent. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.519 percent. The median yield was 4.499 percent, and the low yield was 4.400 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $225 thousand. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $6,000 million. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series C-2011 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 1591, 1118, 1622], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 1634, 1494, 1744], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On October 17, Treasury announced it would auction $19,000 million of 2-year notes of Series V-2003. The issue was to refund $27,693 million of securities maturing October 31 and to pay down about $8,693 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 1749, 1497, 1895], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series V-2003 were dated October 31, 2001 They are due October 31, 2003, with interest payable on April 30 and October 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 2-3/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis. Treasury received tenders for\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 116, 178, 141], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"34\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [630, 116, 1000, 141], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [335, 205, 1295, 243], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER, con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 273, 801, 556], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"the notes before 12 noon e.d.t for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.t. for competitive tenders on October 24. Tenders totaled $43,220 million; Treasury accepted $19,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 2.770 percent with the equivalent price of $99.961. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 86.62 percent. The median yield was 2.740 percent, and the low yield was 2.700 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $749 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $18,251 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 563, 800, 702], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $19,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $6,143 million from Federal Reserve Banks (FRBs) for their own account. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series V-2003 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 717, 446, 750], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Debt Buyback Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 768, 800, 884], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on October 18, 2001, for settlement on October 22, Treasury received $5,632 million of offers. It accepted $1,500 million par amount for a total price paid of $1,788 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 884, 801, 1002], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on October 25, 2001, for settlement on October 29, Treasury received $5,043 million of offers. It accepted $1,000 million par amount for a total price paid of $1,498 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1037, 335, 1070], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"NOVEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1098, 510, 1129], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"November Quarterly Financing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1146, 798, 1289], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"On October 31, Treasury announced it would auction $16,000 million of 5-year notes of Series F-2006 and $7,000 million of 9-3/4-year notes of Series C-2011 to refund $21,588 million of Treasury securities maturing November 15 and to raise about $1,412 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1296, 800, 1438], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series F-2006 were dated November 15, 2001. They are due November 15, 2006, with interest payable on May 15 and November 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 3-1/2 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1440, 801, 1782], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.s.t. for competitive tenders on November 6. Tenders totaled $34,872 million; Treasury accepted $16,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 3.617 percent with an equivalent price of 99.469. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 3.617. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 93.14 percent. The median yield was 3.580 percent, and the low yield was 3.550 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $199 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $15,801 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1787, 800, 1900], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $16,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,799 million from FRBs for their own account. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series F-2006 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 271, 1495, 443], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"The 9-3/4-year 5 percent notes of Series C-2011 were dated August 15, 2001. They were issued November 15, 2001, and are due August 15, 2011, with interest payable on February 15 and August 15 until maturity. Accrued interest of $12.50000 per $1,000, covering the period from August 15 to November 15, 2001, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 450, 1495, 790], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.s.t. for competitive tenders on November 7. Tenders totaled $14,044 million; Treasury accepted $7,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.220 percent with an equivalent price of 106.170. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 83.52 percent. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.220 percent. The median yield was 4.188 percent, and the low yield was 4.135 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $75 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $6,925 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 792, 1495, 908], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $7,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $1,592 million from FRBs for their own account. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series C-2011 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 922, 1122, 950], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 966, 1495, 1080], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"On November 21, Treasury announced it would auction $21,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $28,338 million of securities maturing November 30 and to pay down about $7,338 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 1087, 1495, 1228], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series W-2003 were dated November 30, 2001. They are due November 30, 2003, with interest payable on May 31 and November 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 3 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1235, 1495, 1570], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.s.t. for competitive tenders on November 28. Tenders totaled $31,761 million; Treasury accepted $21,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 3.008 percent with an equivalent price of 99.985. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 14.96 percent. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 3.008 percent. The median yield was 2.960 percent, and the low yield was 2.900 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $774 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $20,226 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1577, 1494, 1662], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $21,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $5,167 million from FRBs for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1678, 1140, 1709], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Debt Buyback Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1725, 1494, 1836], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on November 15, 2001 for settlement on November 19, Treasury received $7,617 million of offers. It accepted $1,750 million par amount for a total price paid of $2,489 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1841, 1494, 1900], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on November 29, 2001, for settlement on December 3, Treasury received $4,654 mil-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [636, 118, 994, 141], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1455, 116, 1486, 141], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"35\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [342, 207, 1290, 243], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER, con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 297, 796, 351], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"lion of offers. It accepted $1,500 million par amount for a total price paid of $2,026 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 389, 330, 417], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"DECEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 446, 417, 471], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 490, 798, 601], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On December 19, Treasury announced it would auction $23,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $24,500 million of securities maturing December 31 and to pay down about $1,500 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 608, 798, 747], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series X-2003 were dated and issued December 31, 2001. They are due December 31, 2003, with interest payable on June 30 and December 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 3-1/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 754, 798, 893], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.s.t. for competitive tenders on December 27. Tenders totaled $55,297 million; Treasury accepted $23,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 297, 1494, 490], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"the high yield of 3.300 percent with an equivalent price of 99.904. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 27.52 percent. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 3.300 percent. The median yield was 3.280 percent, and the low yield was 3.200 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $876 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $22,124 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 500, 1494, 608], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $23,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $6,666 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series X-2003 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [843, 627, 1142, 653], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Debt Buyback Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [843, 665, 1494, 778], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on December 13, 2001 for settlement on December 17, Treasury received $5,393 million of offers. It accepted $1,500 million par amount for a total price paid of $1,728 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [843, 783, 1494, 893], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on December 20, 2001 for settlement on December 24, Treasury received $4,906 million of offers. It accepted $1,250 million par amount for a total price paid of $1,738 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 108, 180, 137], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"36\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [627, 108, 1002, 141], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 189, 1444, 271], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"TABLE PDO-1.\\u2014Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, Dec. 31, 2001\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [171, 288, 1463, 314], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Sources: \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States,\\\" Bureau of the Public Debt, Office of Public Debt Accounting; and Office of Market Finance]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 332, 1495, 1841], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Date of final maturity</th><th>Description (1)</th><th>Issue date (2)</th><th>Total (3)</th><th>U.S. Government and Federal Reserve Banks (4)</th><th>All other investors (5)</th></tr><tr><td>2002</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Jan. 31</td><td>6-1/4%-C note</td><td>01/31/97</td><td>13,453</td><td>1,542</td><td>11,912</td></tr><tr><td>Jan. 31</td><td>1 6-3/8%-R note</td><td>01/31/00</td><td>19,381</td><td>4,225</td><td>15,157</td></tr><tr><td>Feb. 15, 02-07</td><td>7-5/8% bond</td><td>02/15/77</td><td>4,234</td><td>1,566</td><td>2,668</td></tr><tr><td>Feb. 15</td><td>14-1/4% bond</td><td>01/06/82</td><td>1,759</td><td>281</td><td>1,478</td></tr><tr><td>Feb. 28</td><td>6-1/4%-D note</td><td>02/28/97</td><td>13,800</td><td>2,155</