541, 1907], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"May 1, 1967, through June 30, 1970, to E bond buyers.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 106, 177, 139], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"48\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [370, 196, 1257, 238], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Ownership of Federal Securities\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 285, 798, 471], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Federal securities presented in the following tables are public debt securities such as savings bonds, bills, notes and bonds that the Treasury issues. The tables also detail debt issued by other Federal agencies under special financing authorities. [See the Federal debt (FD) tables for a more complete description of the Federal debt.]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 471, 798, 691], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Effective January 1, 2001, Treasury\\u2019s Bureau of the Public Debt revised formats, titles, and column headings in the \\u201cMonthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States,\\u201d Table I: Summary of Treasury Securities Outstanding and Table II: Statutory Debt Limit. These changes should reduce confusion and bring the publication more in line with the public\\u2019s use of terms.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 695, 794, 884], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Treasury's Financial Management Service (FMS) compiles data in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" table OFS-1 from the \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\\\" Effective June 2001, FMS revised procedures and categories in this table to agree with the Bureau of the Public Debt's publication changes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 290, 1494, 476], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Table OFS-1 presents Treasury marketable and non-marketable securities and debt issued by other Federal agencies held by Government accounts, the FRBs and private investors. Social Security and Federal retirement trust fund investments comprise much of the Government account holdings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 481, 1495, 544], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"The FRBs acquire Treasury securities in the market as a means of executing monetary policy.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 549, 1495, 830], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Table OFS-2 presents the estimated amount of public debt securities held by private investors. Information is obtained from sources such as the Federal financial institution regulatory agencies. State, local and foreign holdings include special issues of nonmarketable securities to municipal entities and foreign official accounts. They also include municipal, foreign official and private holdings of marketable Treasury securities. (See footnotes to the table for description of investor categories.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [561, 116, 1069, 139], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"OWNERSHIP OF FEDERAL SECURITIES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1455, 113, 1488, 139], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"49\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 198, 1448, 229], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"TABLE OFS-1.\\u2014Distribution of Federal Securities by Class of Investors and Type of Issues*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [596, 264, 1035, 283], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"descripti