"6\\\">Expenses:</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses/outlays</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Transfers</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total Expenses</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>$85,432</td><td>90,432</td><td>95,432</td><td>100,432</td><td>105,432</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 955, 818, 997], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Estimates for fiscal 2003-2006 are subject to change by appropriation and/or legislative action to reauthorize transfer of motorboat fuel taxes to the Boat Safety Account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1426, 90, 1495, 130], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"139\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [399, 177, 1259, 238], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Oil Spill Liability Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [117, 248, 821, 431], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"The Oil Spill Liability Trust Fund was established on the books of the Treasury by section 8033 of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1986 (Public Law 99-509). It was made effective on January 1, 1990, by section 7811(m)(3) of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1989 (Public Law 101-239) and amended by section 9001 of the Oil Pollution Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-380).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [126, 427, 807, 608], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"Amounts equivalent to the taxes received from the environmental tax on petroleum, but only to the extent of the Oil Spill Liability Trust Fund rate, are appropriated to the fund. The tax is not applied during any calendar quarter if the Secretary of the Treasury estimates that, as of the close of the preceding calendar quarter, the unobligated balance in the fund exceeds $1 billion.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [124, 601, 805, 667], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"Certain amounts were transferred from other funds and were appropriated to the Oil Spill Liability Trust Fund as pro-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 245, 1497, 332], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"vided by 26 United States Code 9509(b). Certain paid penalties and amounts recovered for damages are also appropriated to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 330, 1495, 429], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"Amounts in the fund are available for oil spill cleanup costs and certain other related purposes as provided by appropriations acts or section 6002(b) of the Oil Pollution Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-380).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [821, 422, 1495, 528], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"When the provisions of 26 United States Code 9602(b) are met, amounts available in the fund exceeding outlay requirements are invested in public debt securities. Interest is credited to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 523, 1499, 665], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress, required by 26 United States Code 9602(a), are submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [494, 700, 1151, 771], \"page_id\": 137}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-21.\\u2014Oil Spill Liability Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 2001\", \"description\