on_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [457, 240, 1169, 269], \"page_id\": 114}], \"content\": \"[In thousands of dollars. Source: Office of the Assistant Secretary of the Treasury for Management]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 273, 1481, 1153], \"page_id\": 114}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>Current quarter July 1, 2002, through Sept. 30, 2002</th><th>Fiscal year to date Oct. 1, 2001, through Sept. 30, 2002</th></tr><tr><td><b>Income and expense</b></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Profit (+) or loss (-) on:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange</td><td>-102,555</td><td>493,933</td></tr><tr><td>Adjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations 1</td><td>-30,102</td><td>137,022</td></tr><tr><td>Interest (+) or net charges (-) on:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>SDRs</td><td>29,165</td><td>110,885</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>42,233</td><td>182,869</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange</td><td>72,070</td><td>268,016</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Income from operations</td><td>10,811</td><td>1,192,725</td></tr><tr><td>Net income (+) or loss (-)</td><td>10,811</td><td>1,192,725</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 1183, 809, 1273], \"page_id\": 114}], \"content\": \"1 Beginning July 1974, the International Monetary Fund adopted a technique for valuing the SDRs based on a weighted average of exchange rates for the currencies of selected member countries. The U.S. SDR holdings and allocations are valued on this basis beginning July 1974.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1186, 1468, 1308], \"page_id\": 114}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014 Annual balance sheets for fiscal 1934 through 1940 appeared in the 1940 \\\"Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury\\\" and those for succeeding years appeared in subsequent reports through 1980. Quarterly balance sheets beginning with December 31, 1938, have been published in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\" Data from inception to September 30, 1978, may be found on the statements published in the January 1979 \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1058, 186, 1501, 398], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1346, 422, 1488, 469], \"page_id\": 115}], \"content\": \"Trust Funds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 94, 911, 130], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1444, 99, 1490, 127], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"115\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 205, 1239, 252], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Airport and Airway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 269, 790, 514], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"The Airport and Airway Trust Fund was established on the books of Treasury in fiscal 1971, according to provisions of the Airport and Airway Revenue Act of 1970 [49 United States Code 1742(a), repealed]. The Tax Equity and Fiscal Responsibility Act of 1982 (Public Law 97-248, dated September 3, 1982) reestablished the trust fund in the Internal Revenue Code (26 United States Code 9502) effective September 1, 1982.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 514, 790, 759], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Treasury transfers from the general fund to the trust fund amounts equivalent to the taxes received from transportation of persons and property by air, gasoline and jet fuel used in commercial and noncommercial aircraft, and an international departure tax. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, dated November 5, 1990) increased rates for the excise taxes transferred to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 759, 789, 849], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Treasury bases these transfers on estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury. These are subject to adjustments in later transfers in the amount of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 849, 789, 940], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"The Taxpayers Relief Act of 1997 (Public Law 105-35), effective October 1, 1997, extended the aviation excise taxes for 10 years. The Act included other provisions that:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 950, 794, 1103], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing freight waybill and general aviation fuel/gas taxes. It also retained a special rule applied to flights between the continental United States and Alaska or Hawaii. The $6 departure tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index. Effective fiscal year 2001, the tax is $6.40.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1103, 789, 1294], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Converted the 10 percent ad valorem tax on domestic passenger tickets to a combination of ad valorem/flight segment tax over 3 years, beginning October 1, 1997. Beginning October 1999 through September 30, 2007, the tax is 7.5 percent, plus in 2001, a $2.75 tax per segment.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1304, 789, 1362], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Imposed a new 7.5 percent tax on payments to airlines for frequent flyer and similar awards by banks and\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 266, 1490, 358], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"credit card companies, merchants and frequent flyer program partners, such as other airlines, hotels or rental car companies, and other businesses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 365, 1488, 486], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Increased the current $6 international departure tax to $12 per passenger and added a $12 international arrival tax, indexed to the Consumer Price Index. Effective 2001, the tax is $12.80.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 493, 1488, 556], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Lowered tax rates on flights to certain rural airports to 7.5 percent without a flight segment component.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 563, 1490, 688], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Transferred revenues from the 4.3 cents-per-gallon aviation fuel tax dedicated to reducing the national deficit from the general fund to the Airport and Airway Trust Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 691, 1494, 903], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"When the provisions of 26 United States Code 9602(b) are met, amounts available in the fund exceed outlay requirements, Treasury invests excess amounts in public debt securities and credits the interest to the fund. Additional sums from the general fund also are credited as authorized and made available, by law, if they are needed to meet outlay requirements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 903, 1494, 1115], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Treasury makes available to the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), Department of Transportation (DOT), amounts required for outlays to carry out the Airport and Airway program. The Secretary of the Treasury makes other charges to the trust fund to transfer certain refunds of taxes and certain outfits, under section 34 of the Internal Revenue Code (IRC).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 1117, 1494, 1304], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress, required by 26 U.S.C. 9602 (a), are submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Transportation. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 90, 197, 137], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"116\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [712, 80, 918, 130], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [468, 186, 1160, 271], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-10.\\u2014Airport and Airway Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 2002\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [754, 280, 878, 302], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOT]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 304, 1495, 1195], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Description</th><th>IRC section (26 United States Code)</th><th>Amount</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2001</td><td></td><td>$14,484,489,978</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Receipts:</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Excise taxes (transferred from general fund):</td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel other than gasoline</td><td>4041</td><td>257,882,000</td></tr><tr><td>Gasoline</td><td>4081</td><td>554,432,000</td></tr><tr><td>Transportation by airseats, berths, etc</td><td>4261 (a) (b)</td><td>6,414,511,000</td></tr><tr><td>Use of international travel facilities</td><td>4261 (c)